From ff66520fd8e0542ec41b4e1070f2184219c6a1d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 20:37:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 215/219] fix: the peeled pass loop opened a brace in each #if
 branch and CryFX dropped the whole .cfx

CryFX counts braces on the raw text before preprocessing. The X3511
workaround put a `{` in both the %_RT_QUALITY branch and the stock #else
branch, so the function extent ran past ConeTracePS and the parser hit
`pixoutMRTTrace` where it expected a command ("FXBin parser found token
... (Skipping)"): every technique in Total_Illumination.cfx vanished,
SVOGI included. The brace now sits once after the #endif; the RT branch
is `const int p = 0; if (p == 0)`, the stock branch keeps its `for`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SCUvWGLCsqzm3VNMzp4uiS
---
 Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Total_Illumination.cfx | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Total_Illumination.cfx b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Total_Illumination.cfx
index 9d35377a..23649f84 100644
--- a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Total_Illumination.cfx
+++ b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Total_Illumination.cfx
@@ -1939,12 +1939,15 @@ pixoutMRTTrace ConeTracePS(vtxOutWPOS IN)
 	// body's size ([loop] only turns that into X3531). The pass count is one on this
 	// permutation (see nPassesNum above), so the loop is peeled by hand into its single pass.
 	// Without %_RT_QUALITY the stock `for` in the #else below is what compiles, unchanged.
+	// CryFX counts braces on the RAW text before preprocessing: a `{` in each #if branch
+	// desyncs the function extent and the parser drops every technique in the file.
+	// So the brace is shared after the #endif and the RT branch uses a constant `if`.
 	const int p = 0;
-	{
+	if (p == 0)
 #else
 	for (int p = 0; p < nPassesNum; p++)
-	{
 #endif
+	{
 		int s = (nFramesNum == 2) ? (int(SVO_FrameIdByte.x) & 1) : 0;
 		s += p * nFramesNum;
 
-- 
